      "content": "It is a growing concern that advanced wearable tech could be used for surveillance beyond the stated features. While there isn't definitive public evidence of companies covertly building deep psychological profiles from step and heartbeat data alone, the potential for data aggregation is certainly real. Companies can legally collect vast amounts of biometric data, and ethical oversight often lags behind technological capability in these areas. Always thoroughly review privacy policies to understand exactly how your health and movement data is being used and stored.",
