    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. and think about it... if they have the gait and heart rate, they basically have a fingerprint of your nervous system. and with all the other data they already have from our phones and accounts, they could link it all together. i feel like they're already doing it to test how people react to certain stimuli in real time. like, wouldn't it be trivial for a company with that much money to hide a protocol like that in a firmware update?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
