      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes too much sense. it's like they're turning us into walking sensors for their own research. if they can do this with shoes, what else are they doing? i've been seeing weirdly targeted ads right after i've had a stressful day, and it's almost like they know my heart rate spiked before i even typed anything into a search bar. if this is actually happening, how would anyone even prove it if the evidence is literally buried in encrypted code?",
